## Why This Is Asked

Tests understanding of real-world NUMA memory management, concurrency control, and kernelPage migration mechanisms under contention. Requires designing safe race-free handoffs and measurable tests.

## Key Concepts

- NUMA locality and per-page hotness tracking
- Page pinning during migrations
- Migration queues and synchronization
- TLB shootdown mechanics and batching

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal C-like sketch (pseudo)
typedef struct Page { int hot; int owner_node; int locked; void *addr; } Page;
int migrate_page(Page *p) {
  if (p->locked) return -1;
  p->locked = 1;
  // decide target node (home of owner process)
  p->owner_node = /* target node */ 0;
  // perform remap and update state
  p->hot = 0;
  p->locked = 0;
  return 0;
}
```

