## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of demand paging, synchronization, and simple I/O integration in a minimal kernel.

## Key Concepts
- Page tables and TLB
- Copy-on-write semantics
- Per-page locking and CAS to avoid duplicate fetches
- Read-ahead and fairness under contention

## Code Example
```c
// Pseudo: handle_page_fault(vaddr, proc)
Frame f = alloc_frame();
if (!lock_try_acquire(pte)) return fault_again();
if (pte_present(pte)) { unlock(); return; }
if (pte_backing_file(pte)) {
  io_read_async(pte_file(pte), f->addr, PAGE_SIZE, on_complete); 
} else {
  zero_fill(f->addr, PAGE_SIZE);
  map_page(pte, f->addr);
  unlock();
  wake_up_faulting_thread();
}
```

